    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0452" n="442" xml:id="pg442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.50/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-13T20:00:00-04:00">September 13, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>165. Your 238, September 11, 11 a.m. The Bolivian Minister presented on September
                    9 a memorandum accepting the plan of August 1 and a letter<anchor n="70a"
                        xml:id="d455-f1"/> requesting the designation of a mining expert as soon as
                    possible under point 4 thereof.</p>
                <p>Instructions are being drafted for Vanderburg, mining expert now at Lima, to
                    proceed as soon as practicable. Selection of the other experts under the program
                    is proceeding and you will be informed promptly of definite progress in this
                    respect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d455-f1" n="70a" xml:id="d455-f1-content">
                <p>Letter of September 9, addressed to Laurence Duggan, Adviser on Political
                    Relations, not printed.</p>
            </note>
